# Application

Product logic. Register everything in `DependencyInjection.AddApplication()`.

```text
Features/       vertical slices + Shared/ (DTOs, Repository, Helpers, Services)
AI/             ChatOrchestrator, Agents, Tools, Memory, Workflows
Models/         AI turn shapes, ChatMessageRoles
Utilities/      technical cross-cutting only (crypto) — not slice business logic
```

### Helpers vs Utilities

| | `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` or `Shared/Helpers.cs` | `Application/Utilities/` |
|---|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| **What** | Slice or cross-slice **business** logic | **Technical** plumbing with no slice owner |
| **Examples** | `EmailSettingsMapping`, inbox date parsing for AI tools | `CryptographyHelpers`, `Encrypt()` extensions |
| **Uses entities/DTOs?** | Yes — maps, presets, domain rules | No — algorithms, formats, extensions |
| **Promote** | Handler → slice `Helpers` → `Shared/Helpers` | Add here only when 2+ slices need same technical helper and it is not domain mapping |

**Decision tree:** “Does this belong to one slice’s domain?” → `{Slice}/Helpers.cs`. “Used across slices but still product logic?” → `Shared/Helpers.cs`. “Generic technical helper (crypto, parsing lib-style)?” → `Utilities/`. When unsure, start in handler private and promote.

`WebApp/Utilities/` is separate — UI/auth/cookies only; do not put Application business logic there.

## Features — vertical slices

| Folder | Repository | Entity |
|--------|------------|--------|
| `Users/` | `UserRepository` (wired; promote when reused) | `User` |
| `ChatThreads/` | `ChatThreadRepository` | `ChatThread` |
| `ChatMessages/` | `ChatMessageRepository` (wired; promote when reused) | `ChatMessage` |
| `UserSettings/` | `UserSettingsRepository` | `UserSetting` |
| `Shared/` | `SharedRepository`, `Helpers.cs`, `Services.cs` | — |

Each slice and `Shared/` use the **same file names** where needed: `DTOs.cs`, `Repository.cs`, `Helpers.cs`, `Services.cs`. **All DI** in **`Application/DependencyInjection.cs`**.

```text
Features/{Slice}/
  DTOs.cs
  Repository.cs
  Helpers.cs        when needed
  Services.cs       when needed (slice-local facades)
  Commands/
  Queries/

Features/Shared/
  DTOs.cs
  Repository.cs
  Helpers.cs        cross-slice logic / mapping
  Services.cs       cross-slice facades (UserMailboxService, …)
```

**Least scope first** — full escalation tables in `solution.mdc` (global). Application specifics below.

Mirror Infrastructure and **Slice ↔ Shared**: one `DTOs.cs`, one `Repository.cs`, one `Helpers.cs`, one `Services.cs` per folder — add only when needed. Multiple types live in each file. No one-off `EmailSettingsMapping.cs`-style files.

| File | `{Slice}/` | `Shared/` |
|------|------------|-----------|
| `DTOs.cs` | Slice read shapes | Cross-slice read shapes |
| `Repository.cs` | Promoted EF for slice | Cross-slice EF |
| `Helpers.cs` | Mapping, presets, validation | Cross-slice logic |
| `Services.cs` | Slice-local facades | Cross-slice facades (`UserMailboxService`) |

- Slice repos: `IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext>`; do **not** inherit `SharedRepository`
- **Reads** → slice DTOs via `FromEntity` / `FromEntities`
- **Writes** → accept entities; return DTOs
- **Smallest scope first** — see `solution.mdc`; handler level 1 → slice repo → shared repo

### Escalation (logic + data access)

Promote **logic** and **data access** on separate tracks. Do not mix EF in `Helpers.cs` or slice mapping in `Repository.cs`.

#### Logic escalation

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Handler private** | One use case only | `#region # Private Helpers` on handler (static or instance) |
| **2 — Slice helpers** | 2+ handlers, or handler + repo/UI | `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` |
| **3 — Cross-slice** | Multiple slices | `Features/Shared/Helpers.cs` |

Start in the handler. Move to `{Slice}/Helpers.cs` when reused within the slice. Example: `UserSettings/Helpers.cs` (`EmailSettingsMapping`, `EmailProviderPresets`).

#### Services escalation

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Handler private** | One use case only | Handler or private helper |
| **2 — Slice services** | Reused within slice | `{Slice}/Services.cs` |
| **3 — Shared services** | Cross-slice | `Features/Shared/Services.cs` |

`Helpers` = stateless mapping/logic. `Services` = injectable facades (repos, Infrastructure ports). Example: `UserMailboxService` in `Shared/Services.cs`.

#### Data access escalation

**Smallest scope first** — see `solution.mdc`. Promote to slice repo when a **second consumer** needs the **same** method; promote to Shared when cross-slice.

| Level | When | Where |
|-------|------|--------|
| **1 — Handler private** | Default for new data access | Private `*Async` methods on the **handler class** (alongside `HandleAsync`), in `#region # Private Helpers` last; inject `IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext>` |
| **2 — Slice repo** | Same method promoted from level 1 | `{Slice}/Repository.cs` — class always registered in DI |
| **3 — Shared repo** | Cross-slice query (multiple entity folders) | `Features/Shared/Repository.cs` — inject only when needed |

**Features owns all new EF.** Escalation applies to **handlers only**.

**Outside Features** (`AI/`, `Shared/Services.cs`): **slice repos** for single-slice data; **`SharedRepository`** when a query spans slices. **Never** `IDbContextFactory` outside Feature **handlers**.

| Consumer | Single-slice data | Cross-slice data |
|----------|-------------------|------------------|
| Feature handler | Level 1 private → level 2 slice repo | Level 3 `SharedRepository` |
| `AI/`, `Shared` services | `{Slice}Repository` | `SharedRepository` |

If AI/Services need a method that does not exist yet, add it to the **slice repo** (not private EF in AI). Promote to **Shared** only when a second slice is involved.

`SharedRepository` is not a dump of every AI query — only true cross-slice access.

### Models / DTOs

| Kind | Place |
|------|--------|
| Slice read shape | `Features/{Slice}/DTOs.cs` — `FromEntity`, `AsResponse<T>()` |
| Cross-slice read shape | `Features/Shared/DTOs.cs` |
| Use-case message | `{UseCase}Request` : `ICommand<>` / `IQuery<>` |
| Use-case result | `{UseCase}Response` (may extend slice DTO) |
| AI turn | `Models/AI.cs` |
| App constants | `Models/Constants.cs` (`ChatMessageRoles`) |
| `Result` / `ErrorCode` | `MediatR.Results` |

**Naming:** keep `{UseCase}Request` / `{UseCase}Response` — not `SignInCommand`. CQRS kind = `Commands/` or `Queries/` folder + `ICommand` / `IQuery`.

Do **not** put use-case types or slice DTOs in Infrastructure or WebApp.

### Use-case file order

1. `{UseCase}Request`
2. `{UseCase}Response`
3. `{UseCase}RequestValidator`
4. `{UseCase}RequestHandler`

**References:** `Users/Commands/SignIn.cs` (level 1), `ChatThreads/Queries/GetChatThreadById.cs` (level 2), `ChatMessages/Commands/SendChatMessage.cs` (slice repos + level 1).

### Template A — command (level 1, default)

New data access starts here. Inject `IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext>`. Private instance `*Async` methods on the handler class, in `#region # Private Helpers` after `HandleAsync`.

```csharp
public sealed class SignInRequestHandler(IDbContextFactory<AppDbContext> dbContextFactory)
    : IRequestHandler<SignInRequest, SignInResponse>
{
    public async ValueTask<Result<SignInResponse>> HandleAsync(SignInRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var result = new Result<SignInResponse>();

        #region # Execute
        var session = await FindSessionByEmailAndPasswordAsync(request.EmailId, request.Password, cancellationToken);
        #endregion

        #region # Handle Result
        if (session is null)
            result.Failure(ErrorCode.NotFound, "Invalid Credentials");
        else
            result.Success(session.AsResponse<SignInResponse>());
        #endregion

        return result;
    }

    #region # Private Helpers

    private async Task<SessionDto?> FindSessionByEmailAndPasswordAsync(string emailId, string password, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        await using var ctx = await dbContextFactory.CreateDbContextAsync(cancellationToken);
        // ...
    }

    #endregion
}
```

### Template B — query (level 1)

Same as A with `IQuery<>` under `Queries/`.

### Template C — promoted slice repo (level 2)

Inject slice repo only for methods promoted after reuse. Example: `GetActiveByIdAsync` — used by `GetChatThreadById` and `SendChatMessage`.

```csharp
public sealed class GetChatThreadByIdRequestHandler(ChatThreadRepository chatThreadRepo)
    : IRequestHandler<GetChatThreadByIdRequest, GetChatThreadByIdResponse>
{
    public async ValueTask<Result<GetChatThreadByIdResponse>> HandleAsync(GetChatThreadByIdRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
    {
        var result = new Result<GetChatThreadByIdResponse>();

        #region # Execute
        var chatThread = await chatThreadRepo.GetActiveByIdAsync(request.Id, cancellationToken);
        #endregion

        #region # Handle Result
        if (chatThread is null)
            result.Failure(ErrorCode.NotFound, "Chat thread not found.");
        else
            result.Success(chatThread.AsResponse<GetChatThreadByIdResponse>());
        #endregion

        return result;
    }
}
```

### Data access outside Features

`AI/` and `Features/Shared/Services.cs` inject **slice repos** or **`SharedRepository`** — never `IDbContextFactory`. If a capability needs DB access that is not on a repo yet, add the method to the slice repo first.

| Component | Repos |
|-----------|-------|
| `ChatOrchestrator` | `ChatMessageRepository` (history) |
| `ThreadMemoryService` | `ChatThreadRepository`, `ChatMessageRepository` |
| `UserMailboxService` | `UserSettingsRepository` |

### Handler rules

1. `var result = new Result<T>();` first line
2. `result.Success` / `result.Failure` — instance only
3. `#region # Execute` + `#region # Handle Result` always
4. `#region # Private Helpers` last when handler has level-1 data access (Template A/B)
5. Inject slice repo only for promoted methods (Template C); `SharedRepository` only at level 3

| Repo param | Name |
|------------|------|
| `UserRepository` | `userRepo` |
| `UserSettingsRepository` | `userSettingsRepo` |
| `ChatThreadRepository` | `chatThreadRepo` |
| `ChatMessageRepository` | `chatMessageRepo` |

Inject slice repo only for **promoted** methods; handlers still use `IDbContextFactory` for level-1 access.

Entry: `mediator.SendAsync(new SignInRequest(...))` — pipeline in `mediatr.mdc`.

### Settings naming

| Section | Promoted in repo | Level 1 (handler private) |
|---------|------------------|---------------------------|
| General | `UpdateUserProfileAsync`, password match/update | `GetGeneralSettings` |
| Email | `EmailAccountRepository` (default account) | `SaveEmailSettings` → `EmailAccount` |

